{
  "about": "Every file the app is made of, named once. The laptop's service (src/server.ts) and the Worker (edge/src/edge.ts) serve exactly these, the Worker's build (edge/build.mjs) ships exactly these, and the service worker (public/sw.js) keeps them for when there is no connection. A new file for the app is a line here and nothing else (a new page is its file under pages/, a line in pages/index.js, and a line here). 'kept' says when the service worker keeps a copy: 'installed' is at once, so the app opens offline after one visit; 'used' is when the page first asks for it (a typeface nobody chose is never fetched); 'never' is the service worker itself, which the browser keeps.",
